<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 61,212 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 61,212 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 61,212 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 28,844 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Tuesday	 Sept 2</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   6,453	   2,140</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  54,759	  26,704</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours four were expected to sail and six were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		     8,000	 Frost		   5/9</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,500	 Jin Sheng	     due</p>
<p>Containers		  600	 Song shan	     7/9</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,500	 Maria Topic	   8/9</p>
<p>Sugar		     7,500	 Mehedinti	    10/9</p>
<p>Containers		  200	 Lanka Aruna	  10/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
